WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.767
A reshape round trip is not automatically reversible.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:10.887
If the pivot aggregated transaction rows to monthly totals, unpivoting can only recover those monthly totals.

00:00:10.887 --> 00:00:15.772
It cannot recreate the original transaction IDs or individual amounts.

00:00:15.772 --> 00:00:19.217
The grain that survives is the aggregated grain.

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:26.842
A reshape is reversible only when the transformation preserves enough information to reconstruct the source.

00:00:26.842 --> 00:00:31.917
Aggregation, duplicate collapsing, and dropped NULL cells can make the process lossy.

00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:38.742
Validate row counts, keys, totals, and category coverage before assuming a pivot-unpivot round trip preserves

00:00:38.742 --> 00:00:39.760
everything.
